{"kind":"report","text":"Done. The exact clean head is 073d68c78729dce3db971bbba9bd2bf1464152d8 on request/ci-suite-dedup. No implementation artifacts filed, nothing merged.\n\nCurrent main adb6ec9e is carried; the branch is zero behind and three ahead. The only change against your reviewed head e82d9fff is layout_test.go, twenty lines added and three removed, which I checked with a diff restricted to non-docs paths rather than trusting my own memory of what I touched.\n\nThe four forbidden paths are guarded again, and I proved the guard fires rather than trusting a passing test. A test asserting four things do not exist passes just as happily when it is looking in the wrong place, so I created spike/go.mod and ran it — it failed, naming that path — then removed it and created spike/internal, which failed naming that one, then removed it and confirmed the test passes again. Both mutations were reverted; the worktree is clean.\n\nI also confirmed the four paths are genuinely absent from the tree independently of the test, so a green result means absence rather than a mislocated check.\n\nI corrected the test comment. It said the test pins the two facts neither compilation nor the documentation gates prove, which was true of what it kept and equally true of the four facts it had dropped. It now says what the test asserts, including that compilation proves a path exists and nothing but this proves one stays gone. That is prose matching code, not a design change, and it is the whole reason the removal read as complete when it was not.\n\nWhat I deliberately did not do: I did not restore the required-path list. I agreed in the review that compilation proves those, so re-adding them would be reversing your deduplication rather than repairing the defect I found. I did not widen the guard, and I changed nothing else in the reviewed implementation.\n\nGates at this head: go vet silent; the root package tests pass, which is where both the layout and public-surface pins live; the spike report and spike command tests pass; git diff --check is clean against current main; the worktree is clean.\n\nOne thing worth carrying into your re-review, from the original finding rather than this repair. Of the four paths, spike/go.mod was already caught indirectly — it would drop the spike packages out of the module the single suite runs, and the evidence step fails closed when the named cases are absent, which I verified by feeding it a stripped JSON. The other three were caught by nothing. So this guard is doing unique work for three paths and belt-and-braces for the fourth.","body":{"branch":"request/ci-suite-dedup","head":"073d68c78729dce3db971bbba9bd2bf1464152d8","status":"done"}}